## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · MSTest 4.1 · .NET 10  
**Integration calibration applied:** Class carries `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell 3)

**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)  
**Even for integration tests, hard-coded sleeps create flakiness and slow suites.**

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← 3 seconds of dead wait
```

**Fix — poll with timeout:**
```csharp
var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
{
    if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id)) break;
    await Task.Delay(50);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```
**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures on slow agents; 3 s wasted every run.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell 1)

**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

One branch will **never execute** under current data — hidden testing gap.

**Fix — separate deterministic tests per type:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("pro@example.com", "Pro", 0.15m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("pro@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```
**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — one branch is dead code.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell 4)

**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
// ← No assertion. Passes even if inserts silently fail.
```

**Fix — verify the outcome:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```
**Risk if unfixed:** 0% defect-detection power — the test literally cannot fail on logic bugs.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions, zero diagnostic messages. A failure in CI shows only a line number.

**Fix — add messages:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "Inserted user should be retrievable by email");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip unchanged");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip unchanged");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Database should assign a positive Id on insert");
```
**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage when assertions fail in CI logs.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

| Method | Why it's good |
|--------|--------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert; focused on one behavior |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single assertion, self-documenting |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count (3) is contextually obvious after 3 inserts — not a magic number |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good concurrency test; asserts outcome |
| Setup/Cleanup | In-memory SQLite is hermetic — no Mystery Guest smell |

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Why First |
|----------|-------|-----------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~2 min | Zero defect-detection — highest risk |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Dead branch = hidden gap |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~10 min | Flakiness + 3 s per run |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~3 min | Quality-of-life in CI logs |

**Overall verdict:** 4 of 7 tests are clean and well-structured. The 3 high-severity smells are isolated and straightforward to fix — your suite is in reasonable shape with a focused remediation pass.
